{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the actual plot price on Raebareli Road in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Plot prices vary significantly by zone and legal status. In Zone A (PGI Belt — Vrindavan Yojna area), approved resale plots range from ₹2,500–₹5,500/sqft depending on road width and location. In Zone B (DLF Corridor), DLF Garden City BSP is ₹2,100–₹2,500/sqft; Omaxe Metro City plots are ₹4,500–₹5,000/sqft. In Zone C (Mohanlalganj–Kisan Path), approved societies range ₹1,200–₹2,000/sqft; unapproved land drops to ₹700–₹1,200/sqft. The ₹6,000+ figures you see on portals are blended apartment averages — not plot rates."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Raebareli Road a good investment for plots in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes — specifically Zone B (DLF Corridor) for 3–5 year investors, and Zone A (PGI Belt) for rental income buyers. DLF entry plots are listed at ₹2,100/sqft against ₹5,000–₹10,000/sqft in Gomti Nagar Extension. Kisan Path is open; the PGI and Telibagh flyovers and Vigyan Path are approved but not yet built, and SGPGI is expanding. However Zone C requires very careful verification — significant unapproved inventory exists."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which is better — DLF Garden City or Omaxe Metro City for plots?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Different profiles suit different buyers. DLF Garden City has lower entry (₹2,100/sqft BSP vs ₹4,500/sqft for Omaxe plots) and larger plot sizes (2,700–4,500 sqft). Omaxe Metro City (Kalli Pashchim) offers smaller plot sizes from 1,200 sqft — better for buyers with ₹55–75L budgets. Check the RERA number of the exact phase you are buying on up-rera.in. Visit both and compare distance to your workplace — for SGPGI staff, Zone A plots in Vrindavan Yojna are closest. DLF suits buyers who want larger plots in an established township."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I get a home loan for a plot on Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, for LDA-approved and RERA-registered plots. DLF Garden City, Omaxe Metro City, Suraksha Enclave, Skyom City, and Vrindavan Yojna (UPAVP) all have bank loan approvals from major lenders including SBI, HDFC, ICICI, and Axis Bank. Unapproved Zila Panchayat plots and agricultural land are refused by all banks without exception — this is one of the most reliable ways to filter legal plots: if a bank won't lend on it, you shouldn't buy it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the minimum budget for a legal plot on Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For a legally safe, RERA or LDA approved plot, minimum realistic budget is ₹15–20 lakh for 1,000 sqft in Zone C approved societies or Vrindavan Yojna back-lane resale. For a gated township with full amenities (DLF, Suraksha, Omaxe), budget ₹47 lakh minimum. Below ₹15 lakh, almost all available plots are unapproved or agricultural — the legal risk at that price point is extremely high."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why are plot rates on portals showing ₹6,000/sqft for Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Portal averages like ₹6,050/sqft (99acres) or ₹6,000/sqft (Kalli Pashchim on 99acres) are blended averages covering all property types — apartments, flats, independent houses, and plots combined. Apartment rates in gated societies skew these averages significantly upward. Actual plot-only transaction data shows rates of ₹900–₹5,500/sqft depending on zone and approval status. Always ask for plot-specific comps from actual transactions, not corridor averages."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the risks of buying a plot near SGPGI on Raebareli Road?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The three main risks: (1) unapproved Zila Panchayat colonies sold as residential — no bank loan, demolition risk; (2) agricultural land sold as residential without conversion — cannot build, bank refuses financing; (3) \"Registry ho gayi = safe\" misconception — registration does not validate title, land use, or layout approval. Always verify RERA at up-rera.in, land use at upbhulekh.gov.in, and LDA layout at ldalucknow.in before paying anything."
      }
    }
  ]
}
